175	<article class="pcard"><div class="phead"><span class="pname"><i class="pdot" style="background:#E5E7EB"></i>White / Grey</span><button class="copy" type="button" data-prompt="white" aria-label="Copy the White / Grey recolour prompt"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="5.5" y="5.5" width="8" height="8" rx="1"/><path d="M10.5 5.5v-2a1 1 0 0 0-1-1h-6a1 1 0 0 0-1 1v6a1 1 0 0 0 1 1h2"/></svg><span class="copy-label">Copy</span></button></div><p class="psum">Remap blue to white and neutral grey</p><p class="ptext" id="prompt-white">Convert this image's color palette from deep blue tones to clean white and neutral grayscale tones, keeping everything else identical. Replace the dark navy/royal blue background with a soft light-gray to pale silver gradient (or a deep charcoal gradient if you prefer the cubes to pop brighter). The 3D geometric cubes should shift from cobalt/ultramarine blue to bright white and light grey tones — soft mid-grey in the shadows, clean bright white on the lit faces. Preserve the exact same lighting direction, soft grainy/noisy texture on the cube surfaces, and the frosted gradient effect on top of the cubes — the pure white frost on the upper faces and edges must remain untinted, fading naturally into the light grey. Maintain the same contrast, depth, soft shadows, color grading style, and overall clean atmospheric feel. Do not change the composition, geometry, camera angle, or texture — only remap the blue hues to white/grey.</p></article>
176	</div><p class="sr" role="status" aria-live="polite" id="copy-status"></p></section>
177	<script>
178	document.querySelectorAll('.copy').forEach(function(btn){
179	  btn.addEventListener('click', function(){
180	    var key = btn.dataset.prompt;
181	    var text = document.getElementById('prompt-' + key).textContent;
182	    var label = btn.querySelector('.copy-label');
183	    var done = function(){
184	      label.textContent = 'Copied';
185	      btn.dataset.copied = '1';
186	      document.getElementById('copy-status').textContent = key + ' prompt copied to clipboard';
187	      setTimeout(function(){
188	        label.textContent = 'Copy';
189	        btn.removeAttribute('data-copied');
190	      }, 2000);
191	    };
192	    if (navigator.clipboard && window.isSecureContext) {
193	      navigator.clipboard.writeText(text).then(done).catch(fallback);
194	    } else { fallback(); }
195	    function fallback(){
196	      var ta = document.createElement('textarea');
197	      ta.value = text; ta.setAttribute('readonly','');
198	      ta.style.position = 'fixed'; ta.style.opacity = '0';
199	      document.body.appendChild(ta); ta.select();
200	      try { document.execCommand('copy'); done(); }
201	      catch (e) { label.textContent = 'Select manually'; }
202	      document.body.removeChild(ta);
203	    }
204	  });
205	});
206	</script>
